title: PyCascades 2027 CFP Call for Proposals is now OPEN!
---
author: Eliza Sarobhasa
---
body:

It's finally here! PyCascades 2027 will be taking place once again in the PNW city of Seattle, Washington on the weekend of March 20th-21st, 2027. We're excited to see everyone again for our 9th year of the conference, and our first step to getting ready is launching our CFP Call for Proposals!

https://pretalx.com/pycascades-2027/cfp

As we always do, we love proposals from:
- People who've never spoken before (we've got mentors for you!)
- People new to Python
- People who use Python in their spare time
- People who want to talk about something that isn't specifically Python

Schedule: 
- CFP Opens: September 21, 2026
- CFP Closes: October 26, 2026 Anywhere on Earth (UTC -12:00)
- Speaker Invitations Sent: Week of November 20th, 2026
- Conference dates: March 20th & 21st, 2027

Submission Guidelines:
- As you're writing your proposal, keep in mind:
- There are two options for length: 25 minutes and 40 minutes. Make sure to select the correct option for your talk!
- All presentations are in-person in Seattle, WA.
- We will have a session chair introduce you beforehand.
- There will not be a Q&A after the talk. We encourage attendees to ask questions and discuss in the hallway between talks.
- By submitting a proposal, you agree to follow the PyCascades Code of Conduct.

Read more information on the CFP process here
https://pretalx.com/pycascades-2027/cfp

We will be posting an update in a few on our upcoming "How to submit a PyCascades CFP" in collaboration with PyLadies in late September. Keep an eye on our blog, socials, Slack, or newsletter to stay up to date!
---
pub_date: 2026-09-21
